[template main()]
=== MTL Macro Examples ===

[section('Introduction')]
Macros allow you to define reusable text blocks with parameters.
They are perfect for formatting, wrappers, and repeated structures.
[/section]

[section('Code Example')]
Here's how to use the codeBlock macro:

[codeBlock('swift')]
func greet(name: String) {
    print("Hello, \(name)!")
}
[/codeBlock]
[/section]

[section('Emphasis Example')]
You can [emphasis()]emphasize important text[/emphasis] using macros!
[/section]

Macros are useful for:
- Consistent formatting
- Reducing duplication
- Creating reusable templates
[/template]
